      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "BOOM BAM RANGER (8) continues to race well, filling the minors at the last three starts, the latest at Richmond in 36.22. Goes well from this draw. Boxed wide but will go close with the right run. STILTON SHINE (7) hit the ground running from the squeeze draw with a fast early split last time, but run over late and missed the frame when a 2.75 lengths fourth (42.73) over 720m at this track. Great chance to atone. LOCO KADE (4) was strongly supported last start when a short priced favourite and duly saluted winning by a nose at Richmond in a handy 36.29. Jumping from the pinch draw but in form and has the ability. The form from her last run is stacking up nicely. One of main contenders. RAYMAR SHAME (2) is worth consideration.",
